   "source": [
    "# HORECA Zomato Market Intelligence – Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Project Type:** Summer Internship / Academic Data Analysis Project  \n",
    "**Domain:** Hospitality, Restaurant & Food Service (HORECA)  \n",
    "**Dataset:** Zomato Restaurant & Menu Dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "**Team Name:** Team NeuroNauts  \n",
    "**Submitted by(Team):** Sudip Chakraborty, Vivek Khamaru, Shreya Adhikari, Rakesh Kastha  \n",
    "**College:** Government College of Engineering and Ceramic Technology  \n",
    "**Department:** Information Technology (IT)  \n",
    "**Academic Year:** 2026  \n",
    "**Guide:** Arijit Midya\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Project Objective\n",
    "\n",
    "The objective of this project is to analyse the Zomato dataset using Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) techniques and identify potential business opportunities for a new food venture.\n",
    "\n",
    "The analysis focuses on three key business decisions:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Cuisine Selection:** Identifying promising cuisine categories based on restaurant competition, customer engagement, ratings and pricing.\n",
    "2. **City and Neighbourhood Selection:** Evaluating potential markets and locations based on restaurant density, customer engagement and ratings.\n",
    "3. **Dining vs. Delivery Strategy:** Comparing dining and delivery ratings and customer engagement to determine a suitable service model.\n",
    "\n",
    "The study applies data cleaning, descriptive statistics, univariate, bivariate and multivariate analysis, geographical comparison, outlier detection, correlation analysis and statistical hypothesis testing to derive meaningful insights and data-driven business recommendations.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Project Scope\n",
    "\n",
    "This project is based on Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) and business intelligence. It aims to identify market patterns, understand customer preferences, compare restaurant performance and recommend potential opportunities using the available dataset.\n",
    "\n",
    "The findings are indicative and should be further validated through market research, operational costs and real-world business conditions.\n"
   ]
  },
