    "## 6. Channel analysis – ratings, votes and statistical test\n",
    "\n",
    "Use one paired observation per restaurant. Pearson correlation describes linear association; a paired t-test checks whether the mean within-restaurant rating difference is zero. Statistical significance is not the same as commercial importance. Vote counts are highly skewed/zero-heavy, so compare medians and non-zero counts as well as means.\n"
   ]
  },
