   "source": [
    "## 8. Business interpretation and recommendations\n",
    "\n",
    "### Cuisine\n",
    "- **Desserts:** balanced mainstream choice – approximately 90 outlet-cuisine entries, 3.93 average rating, 185 median total votes and ₹220 median item price.\n",
    "- **Kebab:** niche pilot – approximately 12 outlet-cuisine entries, 3.90 average rating, 422.5 median votes and ₹240 median item price. This is a much smaller sample and should be validated locally.\n",
    "\n",
    "### City and micro-market\n",
    "- **Ahmedabad** is the demand-led underserved candidate: 74 restaurants, 3.85 average rating, 186 median votes and only 19/74 restaurants rated at least 4.0.\n",
    "- **C G Road** is a micro-market pilot candidate: four restaurants overall, average rating around 4.04 and median votes around 410.5. The supplied data shows one dessert outlet there with roughly 3.95 rating and 363 votes. This is a very small sample.\n",
    "- **Pune** is a strong alternative if the priority is a higher city rating and a smaller overall restaurant count.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Channel\n",
    "Delivery ratings are materially higher on average, but delivery votes are non-zero for fewer restaurants and the median delivery vote count is zero. Start delivery-friendly with a limited dine-in option; measure real orders, repeat purchase and contribution margin before committing to delivery-only.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Limitations\n",
    "The data does not contain operating costs, rent, commissions, actual sales, gross margins, customer demographics or dates. Zomato votes are engagement proxies and prices are listed menu prices, not realized revenue. No profitability claim can be proved from these fields alone.\n"
   ]
